# Intent: The owner found Simon Says (text only, sensors only) overlapped with Do It and prefers buttons. Simon Says is removed from the player and from the app image (pack list 7 to 6 games). Do It is now a button game: its pack (firmware/games/bopit.json, a data file) shows six large tiles (Tap, Swipe left, Swipe right, Shake, Pet head, Tilt) under the call-out, and pressing the matching tile or doing the physical move counts. Rock Paper Scissors becomes three full-height tiles (94 by 130 px, tap anywhere in one) with large drawn hands and scissors, a countdown beat (rock, paper, scissors, shoot), a short sound per choice, funny win, tie and lose sounds and a face reaction (a data pack, firmware/games/rps.json); the pack limit for shapes goes from 48 to 64 for it. Every game then uses on-screen buttons or tiles.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_games.cc (ours, G02, UI13) and firmware/main/CMakeLists.txt (ours, G01, UI13)
# Check after a flash: the Games page lists six games with no More tile; Do It shows a call-out and six tiles, the called tile lights up, and pressing it (or swiping, shaking, petting, tilting as called) scores; no Simon Says anywhere.
# Kconfig: none

